  "notes": "Formovie / Fengmi projector MiProjM05 (device eva, Amlogic/droidlogic), Android TV 9 (SDK 28), build PQ3B.190705.003.2102\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<projector ip> tools/disable.sh examples/formovie-mprojm05/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<projector ip> tools/restore.sh examples/formovie-mprojm05/debloat.txt com.google.android.tvlauncher\nEverything is DISABLED for user 0, never uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nStock launcher: com.google.android.tvlauncher. Only other HOME claimant is com.android.tv.settings/.system.FallbackHome.\nSaved Wi-Fi belongs to android.uid.system and com.google.uid.shared, not setupwraith, which does not claim HOME here.\nThe firmware re-enables com.google.android.leanbacklauncher at every boot; it claims no HOME, so it is left alone.\nHDMI comes from com.droidlogic.tvinput, so the launcher's Inputs pill lists the one HDMI port. No tuner:\nlive_tv_package can be left empty.\nKept: com.fengmi.projector.imaging (focus, keystone, auto keystone; auto keystone still works with Camera2 off),\ncom.fengmi.fmsettings, com.fengmi.platform, com.formovie.fmutils, com.formovie.gsettings (projector settings,\nvoice key, USB), com.formovie.launchboard (Formovie app drawer), droidlogic services, Live Channels, Play Store and Services.\nRemote (\"Xiaomi RC\", Vendor_2717_Product_32b9.kl): the gear button sends KEY_APPSELECT (580), mapped to\nKEYCODE_ALL_APPS (284), not KEY_TAPE (384). With tvlauncher disabled it does nothing; settings_key_keycodes 284 with\nHOME_KEY_SERVICE=1 makes it open Settings, but that helper stops a held Volume Up from ramping (one step per press).\nFirmware updates come through TvSettings; no separate updater package.\nTelemetry and partner auto-installs",
